❓ Step 9: Common Student Confusions
❌ “Context replaces Redux”

👉 Clarify:

Context = data sharing
Redux = state management system
❌ “Redux is always better”

👉 Clarify:

Overkill for small apps
❌ “Context has no performance issues”

👉 Explain:

Re-renders happen



Context lets any component directly access shared data without passing props step-by-step.

Super Simple Summary
🧵 Prop Drilling → pass data step by step
🌐 Context → share data globally (no props)
🏪 Redux → manage complex global state with rules
🎯 Easy Rule for Students
Small app → Prop Drilling
Medium app → Context
Large app → Redux

